%% Cross-deployment recovery (M1 mechanism).
%% Two vLLM deployments attached to one HMPM. Deployment A loses HBM.
%% Deployment B detects A is orphaned, claims A's blocks, prefetches them.
%% See docs/design/rfcs/exclusive-tiered-caching.md §5
sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    participant A as vLLM deployment A
    participant HMPM as Host Memory Pool Manager
    participant B as vLLM deployment B
    participant Drv as B's CrossDeploymentRecoveryDriver

    Note over A,B: Steady state — both deployments serving
    A->>HMPM: heartbeat (1 Hz)
    B->>HMPM: heartbeat (1 Hz)
    A->>HMPM: allocate(FAST_CPU, keys=[k1, k2])
    HMPM-->>A: physical block ids
    Note over A,HMPM: A stores KV blocks for in-flight requests

    Note over A: A's accelerator dies — heartbeats stop
    HMPM->>HMPM: heartbeat timeout reached<br/>mark deployment_id=A as orphaned

    Note over B,Drv: External orchestrator notifies B<br/>which request_ids to recover
    Drv->>B: recover(peer="A", request_ids=[r1])
    Drv->>B: compute_offload_keys(r1) → [k1, k2]
    Drv->>HMPM: lookup_peer(keys=[k1, k2])
    HMPM-->>Drv: PeerHit(k1, FAST_CPU, blk_id), PeerHit(k2, ...)
    Drv->>HMPM: claim_orphan(peer="A", keys=[k1, k2])
    HMPM-->>Drv: ownership transferred to B
    Drv->>B: absorb_claimed_keys(keys, medium="FAST_CPU")

    Note over B: Next prefix-cache lookup hits;<br/>existing load path moves blocks → HBM
    B->>HMPM: (cpu_to_gpu_handler reads via existing pool slice)
    Note over B: B resumes A's in-flight requests, no re-prefill
